#
# Counter-example for the operator-signature gate: a math:ArithmeticOperation
# individual that declares its math:operatorDomain but OMITS its
# math:operatorCodomain (sh:minCount 1, derived from the exact-one
# math:operatorCodomain restriction on the math:ArithmeticOperation class).
# Validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:UnframedOperator).
# The domain is present, so the missing codomain is the single isolated violation —
# an operator is not a bare glyph; it carries its full signature over number systems.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecOperatorMissingCodomain).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:halfSignedOperator a math:ArithmeticOperation ;
    math:operatorDomain math:realNumbers .
